# Adopt repository-local agent governance

- Status: implemented
- Date: {{ADOPTION_DATE}}
- Owners: {{DECISION_OWNERS}}

## Decision

Adopt a minimal repository-local governance layer with explicit fact owners, Agent Notes for durable decisions, Active Work for temporary cross-session state, and project Skills for reusable workflows.

## Context

{{ADOPTION_CONTEXT}}

## Alternatives

- Keep guidance only in task conversations. Rejected because durable boundaries would not be discoverable in later work.
- Generate a comprehensive framework independent of repository evidence. Rejected because speculative policy would misdescribe the implementation.

## Consequences

- Governance starts with the smallest evidenced implementation and grows through real use.
- Existing project rules remain authoritative at their established scope.
- New durable facts require one owner; other documents link that owner.

